 852+ B42A              ; ================================================================
 853+ B42A              ; Extraction services. Both write a byte range into a new file in the
 854+ B42A              ; active panel directory; they differ only in where the bytes come from.
 855+ B42A              ;
 856+ B42A              ; SERVICE_EXTRACT takes them from the loaded data pages, so a plugin can
 857+ B42A              ; write back data it has modified in RAM (the editor saves this way).
 858+ B42A              ; SERVICE_EXTRACT_SEEK re-reads them from the source file instead, which
 859+ B42A              ; is the only way to reach data past the 64KB the viewer keeps in RAM
 860+ B42A              ; (TRD disk images are up to 640K).
 861+ B42A              ; The shared steps live in view_extract_prepare/open_dest/exit.
 862+ B42A              ; ================================================================
 863+ B42A
